[h1]Flavorium Universalis v0.3.9 Hotfix[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.3.* | Multiplayer synchronized[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Stable release now on EU5 1.3[/h2]

The stable mod moves to EU5 1.3 with this update. The 1.3 work that lived on the beta branch is now the main release, so the stable Workshop item covers 1.3 and the separate beta item is no longer needed to play on the current patch.

[h2]New: Custom Subject Types game rule[/h2]

A new [b]C&C: Custom Subject Types[/b] game rule (default: on) toggles the mod's custom subject types. It gates every advance that unlocks one, along with the estate privileges and government reforms bundled with them, so a disabled subject can neither be researched nor created and its event chains stay dormant.

[list]
[*] [b]Enabled:[/b] every country can research the advances that unlock the custom subjects.
[*] [b]Player Only:[/b] only human-controlled countries can; the AI keeps to vanilla subject types.
[*] [b]Disabled:[/b] the unlocking advances never appear, so the custom subjects cannot be created.
[/list]
